This directory is vendored from choudoufu
(https://github.com/INTENTIUS/choudoufu), internal/live/staterecord, at commit
17c6f0a7ea616ebe3f9ec2a7f2c397e6e09c2b94.

Every .go file here is covered by the Mozilla Public License, version 2.0,
file by file, as its own header says (SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0). The
MPL text is at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/. The rest of this repository is
Apache-2.0; MPL-2.0 is file-level, so the two sit side by side and nothing
outside this directory takes on the MPL.

Files carried unchanged: azureblob.go, azurecontract.go, bucketcontract.go,
bucketowner.go, bulk.go, contract.go, denied.go, doc.go, gcs.go, gcscontract.go,
kmsdenied.go, kubernetes.go, kubernetesadmission.go, kubernetescontract.go,
kubernetescontrolplane.go, objecttags.go, s3.go, store.go.

estate-boundary.yaml is choudoufu's live/kubernetes/estate-boundary.yaml at the
same commit, carried unchanged.

Files modified for plunge (each stays MPL-2.0):

  kubernetesboundary.go  reads the shipped estate boundary through
               EstateBoundaryYAML in this package (estateboundary.go) in
               place of choudoufu's live/kubernetes package.
  estateboundary.go  choudoufu's live/kubernetes/embed.go, moved into this
               package, since an embed directive can only reach files under
               its own package's directory.
  local.go     PutIfAbsent writes a temp file and hard-links it into place
               instead of an O_CREATE|O_EXCL open followed by a write, so a
               concurrent Get never reads the empty file (found by
               TestTwoFirstRunsConvergeOnOneDefaultProvider; choudoufu's copy
               has the same race).

Not carried: runcache.go, counting.go, versions.go, testing.go and every
_test.go file. The Kubernetes store was added in INTENTIUS/plunge#14 (the
ruling there), behind plunge's plunge+k8s:// opener.

doc.go describes the package as choudoufu wrote it, OpenTofu references
included. plunge's own use of the store is documented in
pkg/backend/plunge/doc.go.
